VyomFix Aviation Simulation Compliance Reference Document

National Aviation Authority – Flight Simulation Compliance Requirements

Section 1: General Requirements
1.1 The simulation system must accurately reproduce the flight dynamics of the reference aircraft.
1.2 All data used for validation must be traceable to real flight test data.

Section 2: Flight Path and Position
2.1 The simulated Northing, Easting, and Altitude must not deviate from real flight data by more than 5% at any time.
2.2 The mean deviation for position parameters must not exceed 2%.

Section 3: Attitude and Orientation
3.1 Euler angles (Roll, Pitch, Heading) must remain within ±3 degrees of real flight data.
3.2 The mean deviation for attitude parameters must not exceed 1.5 degrees.

Section 4: Acceleration and Forces
4.1 Simulated accelerations (X, Y, Z, Total) must not deviate from real data by more than 10% at any time.
4.2 The mean deviation for acceleration parameters must not exceed 5%.

Section 5: Anomaly Reporting
5.1 Any instance where a parameter exceeds the allowed deviation must be reported, with time, value, and possible cause.
5.2 The system must provide a mapping of each anomaly to the relevant compliance section. 